---
layout: base.njk
title: Home
description: "Acme Apps — small, focused apps that do one thing well. Cyclometer, RADAR.speed and DockClockX are coming soon."
---
<section class="hero full-bleed">
  <picture>
    <img
      class="hero__img"
      src="/assets/img/coyote-1200.webp"
      srcset="/assets/img/coyote-1200.webp 1200w, /assets/img/coyote-2400.webp 2400w"
      sizes="100vw"
      width="2400"
      height="1600"
      alt="A coyote standing on a gravel road in the desert, looking back over its shoulder"
      fetchpriority="high">
  </picture>

  <div class="hero__inner">
    <div class="hero__text">
      <h1>{{ site.title }}</h1>
      <p class="lead">{{ site.description }}</p>
      <p>
        We build for people who move — on two wheels, on foot, on the road.
        Nothing is shipping yet. Here is what is on the way.
      </p>
      <a class="button" href="#apps">See what&rsquo;s coming</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="hero__credit">
    Photo by <a href="https://unsplash.com/photos/bgSKRrYFYxc">Joshua Wilking</a> on Unsplash
  </p>
</section>

<section class="apps-section" id="apps" aria-labelledby="apps-title">
  <h2 id="apps-title">Coming soon</h2>

  <ul class="apps">
    <li class="app">
      <img class="app__icon" src="/assets/img/cyclometer.svg" width="72" height="72" alt="">
      <div class="app__body">
        <h3 class="app__name">
          <a class="app__link" href="https://cyclometer.app/">Cyclometer</a>
        </h3>
        <p class="app__badge">Coming soon</p>
        <p class="app__desc">
          A cycling computer that stays out of the way. Speed, distance, and
          elevation, recorded cleanly and kept on your device. Also, there is no
          app login. Use the services you already love like Strava and Ride with
          GPS with ease. Pricing at $10. Not a subscription, forever!
        </p>
        <p class="app__more" aria-hidden="true">cyclometer.app &rarr;</p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="app">
      <img class="app__icon" src="/assets/img/radar-speed.svg" width="72" height="72" alt="">
      <div class="app__body">
        <h3 class="app__name">RADAR.speed</h3>
        <p class="app__badge">Coming soon</p>
        <p class="app__desc">
          Read the road behind you. Pair a radar unit and check the speed of
          traffic like &ldquo;Ponch&rdquo;. Free utility for everyone.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="app">
      <img class="app__icon" src="/assets/img/dockclockx.webp" width="72" height="72" alt="">
      <div class="app__body">
        <h3 class="app__name">DockClockX</h3>
        <p class="app__badge">Coming soon</p>
        <p class="app__desc">
          Why doesn't your Mac have a nice visual clock to look at? In the past,
          NeXTSTEP displayed the time in the dock. This app lets your Mac do the
          same.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
